<%# D3: the app states how long it keeps a document rather than leaving it
    implied. Unlike its predecessor this app writes files to disk, so the
    promise is worth stating precisely.

    No clock time. The server runs in UTC and has no reliable way to know the
    reader's zone, so a formatted time was not their local time at all — it read
    as "5:40 PM" to someone whose morning it still was. A duration is correct in
    every zone (R3.3, D1).

    With a document the sentence ends in a phrase the retention controller
    replaces with a live countdown. Without JavaScript it stands on its own and
    still states the promise (R3.5). The period comes from Document::RETENTION,
    so the promise and the behaviour cannot drift apart. %>
<p class="text-lead text-ink-muted text-center mt-10">
  <% if document %>
    This document and related data will be deleted
    <span data-retention-target="remaining"><%= Document::RETENTION.inspect %> after you added it</span>.
  <% else %>
    Your document and everything we work out from it will be removed
    <%= Document::RETENTION.inspect %> after you add it.
  <% end %>
</p>
